  "genie_instructions": "DOMAIN CONTEXT\nThis space supports Design Space Exploration for a fabless chip-design company taping out 20 designs across 3nm/5nm/7nm/14nm nodes in 5 design families (Application Processor, AI Accelerator, RF Modem, IoT Controller, Power Management). EDA simulation runs sweep PPA (Power-Performance-Area) tradeoffs. Stakeholders include Physical Design teams (timing slack, DRC), Architecture (Pareto fronts, power-performance scoring), and the VP of Engineering (design closure status, tapeout readiness). DRC violations and timing slack are the two hard gates for tapeout.\n\nMETRIC DEFINITIONS\n- Timing slack = timing_slack_ns; \u22650 = timing met, <0 = WNS violation\n- Dynamic power = dynamic_power_mw; mobile SoC target <500 mW, edge AI <2000 mW\n- Leakage power = leakage_power_mw; advanced-node thermal driver\n- Die area = die_area_mm2; mass-volume parts target <100 mm\u00b2\n- DRC violations = drc_violations; must equal 0 to tapeout\n- Pareto-optimal = pareto_optimal flag in parameter_explorations\n- Convergence rate = convergence_pct; >80% indicates healthy optimization closure\n- Design closure status = design_closure_status; On Track / At Risk / Behind Schedule / Blocked\n\nQUERY GUIDANCE\n- ALWAYS prefer metric views with MEASURE() syntax for aggregations.\n  - simulation_run_metrics (source: simulation_runs) \u2014 dims: run_date, design_family, run_status, target_node_nm; measures: total_simulation_runs, completed_runs, avg_dynamic_power_mw, avg_die_area_mm2, avg_drc_violations, total_timing_slack_ns, total_leakage_power_mw, unique_design_count, max_timing_slack_ns.\n  - optimization_result_metrics (source: optimization_results) \u2014 dims: result_month, design_family, design_closure_status; measures: avg_best_power_mw, avg_best_performance, avg_convergence_pct, total_optimization_records, blocked_design_count, total_best_area_mm2, unique_design_count, max_best_power_mw, total_pareto_front_size.\n- Use GROUP BY ALL with MEASURE() queries.\n- For monthly trends, always wrap the date in DATE_TRUNC('month', <date_col>).\n- For \"Top X\" requests, return LIMIT 10 unless the user specifies otherwise.\n- Query base tables directly only when needing columns not exposed by metric views (e.g. design_id, design_name, clock_freq_ghz, supply_voltage_v, pareto_optimal, best_performance_score).\n- When the user's phrasing matches a SQL snippet display name (filters, expressions, or measures), prefer that snippet.",
  "sample_questions": [
    "Which 10 designs have the highest average DRC violations in the trailing 12 months?",
    "Show monthly trend of completed simulation runs by design family.",
    "Which design families have the most Blocked designs this quarter \u2014 what is blocking tapeout?",
    "Top 10 designs by best performance score this month, with their power and area tradeoffs.",
    "How has average convergence percentage trended month-over-month by design family?",
    "Which target process nodes have the worst average timing slack \u2014 where are we missing closure?",
    "What is the total leakage power across all 5nm and 3nm designs, and how does that trend monthly?"
  ],
  "example_sqls": [
    {
      "question": "How many distinct transactions appeared each month?",
      "sql_lines": [
        "SELECT DATE_TRUNC('month', run_date) AS month, COUNT(DISTINCT transaction) AS distinct_count",
        "FROM {fqn}.simulation_runs",
        "GROUP BY 1",
        "ORDER BY 1"
      ]
    },
    {
      "question": "How has highest timing slack ns changed over time?",
      "sql_lines": [
        "SELECT run_date, MEASURE(max_timing_slack_ns) AS max_timing_slack_ns",
        "FROM {fqn}.simulation_run_metrics",
        "GROUP BY ALL",
        "ORDER BY run_date"
      ]
    },
    {
      "question": "How many distinct forecasts appeared each month?",
      "sql_lines": [
        "SELECT DATE_TRUNC('month', result_month) AS month, COUNT(DISTINCT forecast) AS distinct_count",
        "FROM {fqn}.optimization_results",
        "GROUP BY 1",
        "ORDER BY 1"
      ]
    },
    {
      "question": "Which chip designs have the highest total *?",
      "sql_lines": [
        "SELECT design_name, SUM(*) AS record_count, SUM(target_node_nm) AS total_target_node_nm",
        "FROM {fqn}.simulation_runs",
        "WHERE run_status = 'Completed'",
        "GROUP BY design_name",
        "ORDER BY total_target_node_nm DESC",
        "LIMIT 10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "question": "How has total target clock frequency in ghz trended over time?",
      "sql_lines": [
        "SELECT snapshot_date, SUM(clock_freq_ghz) AS total_clock_freq_ghz",
        "FROM {fqn}.parameter_explorations",
        "GROUP BY snapshot_date",
        "ORDER BY snapshot_date"
      ]
    },
    {
      "question": "How does best performance score achieved compare across chip designs?",
      "sql_lines": [
        "SELECT design_name, AVG(best_performance_score) AS avg_best_performance_score",
        "FROM {fqn}.optimization_results",
        "GROUP BY design_name",
        "ORDER BY design_name",
        "LIMIT 10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "question": "How has total leakage power mw changed over time?",
      "sql_lines": [
        "SELECT run_date, MEASURE(total_leakage_power_mw) AS total_leakage_power_mw",
        "FROM {fqn}.simulation_run_metrics",
        "GROUP BY ALL",
        "ORDER BY run_date"
      ]
    }
  ],
